diff --git a/os/system/modules/file/delete.notes.md b/os/system/modules/file/delete.notes.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..fd5f44bad
--- /dev/null
+++ b/os/system/modules/file/delete.notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+Only when the step names a file or a folder to delete: `delete file %x%`, `remove file 'a.txt'`, `delete the folder 'tmp'`. A bare `remove %x%` removes the variable (variable.remove), even when %x% holds a file — the file stays on disk.
+Path — the file or folder to delete, as the step writes it.
diff --git a/os/system/modules/variable/remove.notes.md b/os/system/modules/variable/remove.notes.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..7e286d59a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/os/system/modules/variable/remove.notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+`remove %x%` removes the variable %x%, whatever it holds — a file it holds stays on disk. Deleting the file itself needs the word: `delete file %x%` is file.delete.
